meta {
  name: Get Trust Bundle (validate SVID JWKS)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{SWA_API_BASE}}/api/swa/trust-domains/{{TRUST_DOMAIN_NAME}}/.well-known/jwks
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # Workload SVID Test (JWT-SVID)

  The **SVID fetch is not HTTP** - it is done via the SWA Agent's Workload API over a Unix
  socket (`/tmp/swa-agent/public/api.sock`), so it runs as a Pod in the cluster (kubectl),
  not in Bruno. This HTTP request fetches the **trust domain JWKS** (public keys that
  VALIDATE the JWT-SVID), and serves as a home for documenting the full test.

  ## Prerequisite (important)
  The Pod must match the `workload_registration_policy` of the node group `k8s-prod-ng`:
  `k8s.ns == 'swa-server' && k8s.sa == 'swa-server'`. That is why the Pod runs in
  namespace `swa-server` with SA `swa-server`. In any other ns/sa the agent DENIES issuance.
  The Pod must also land on a node that has the swa-agent running (DaemonSet, 4/4 nodes).

  ## Manifest (saved in ../svid-fetcher.yaml)
  apiVersion: v1
  kind: Pod
  metadata:
    name: svid-fetcher
    namespace: swa-server
    labels:
      app.kubernetes.io/name: svid-fetcher
  spec:
    restartPolicy: Never
    serviceAccountName: swa-server
    containers:
      - name: svid-fetcher
        image: docker.io/YOUR_REGISTRY/swa-agent:1.0.0-amd64
        args: [api, fetch, jwt, --audience=conjur, --socketPath=/tmp/swa-agent/public/api.sock, --output=json]
        volumeMounts:
          - name: agent-socket
            mountPath: /tmp/swa-agent
    volumes:
      - name: agent-socket
        hostPath:
          path: /tmp/swa-agent
          type: Directory

  ## Run and view the SVID
  - kubectl apply -f svid-fetcher.yaml
  - kubectl logs svid-fetcher -n swa-server      (JSON output with svids[] + bundles[])
  - kubectl delete pod svid-fetcher -n swa-server

  ## Returned SVID (decoded claims)
  - sub (SPIFFE ID): spiffe://example.machineid/k8s-prod-ng/ns/swa-server/sa/swa-server
  - iss: https://YOUR_SWA_API_HOST/api/swa/trust-domains/example.machineid
  - aud: conjur   (controlled by --audience)
  - validity: 300s (alg RS512)

  The `sub` confirms the chain: trust domain -> node group -> workload ns/sa.
  To allow other workloads, adjust the node group's workload_registration_policy.
}
